@startuml
title NetGuard - Network Traffic Processing

autonumber

actor "End User" as User
participant "Dashboard" as UI
participant "REST API" as API
participant "PCAP Importer" as Source
queue "Message Broker" as Broker
participant "Flow Processor" as Processor
participant "Detection Engine" as Detector
database "Database" as DB

User -> Source: Import PCAP / flow file

loop For each network flow
    Source -> Broker: Publish flow
    Broker -> Processor: Deliver flow
    Processor -> Processor: Update window statistics
end

Processor -> Detector: Submit network flows
Detector -> Detector: Analyze time windows
Detector -> Detector: Apply rules and statistical/ML methods

alt Anomaly detected
    Detector -> Detector: Classify anomaly and generate evidence
    Detector -> DB: Store detection result and alert
else Normal traffic
    Detector -> DB: Store processed flow data
end

User -> UI: View monitoring dashboard
UI -> API: GET /api/alerts and /api/statistics
API -> DB: Query alerts and statistics
DB --> API: Results
API --> UI: Response
UI --> User: Display alerts and network statistics

@enduml